# Build context exclusions. Everything here would be sent to the Docker
# daemon on every build, slowing it down and bloating the context.
#
# venv/ is the important one: without this, your entire local virtualenv
# (hundreds of MB, built for YOUR machine) is uploaded to the daemon on
# every single build.

.git
.gitignore
.github
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

venv/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.db
*.sqlite3
*.log

# The test suite and helper scripts are not in the image. The Dockerfile
# only COPYs `app/`, `alembic/`, and `alembic.ini`, so these never enter
# the image regardless - excluding them just trims the context upload.
tests/
scripts/
docs/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
coverage.xml

README.md
DECISIONS.md
LICENSE

# Editor / OS noise. Harmless in the image, but there is no reason to
# upload them on every build.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Other Python project files. If any of these ever appear at the repo
# root, they must not silently enter the context.
pyproject.toml
requirements.txt

# NOTE: `.dockerignore` itself and `Dockerfile` are intentionally NOT
# listed. The build client needs to read both, and excluding them does
# not reduce the context.
#
# NOTE: requirements-prod.txt is deliberately NOT excluded - the
# Dockerfile COPYs it in two separate stages.